fix(web): gate detailed circuit errors and stream/cache map tiles

Close two web-host hardening gaps before release.

- DetailedErrors: interactive-circuit exception messages and stack traces
  were streamed to browsers in every environment. Gate DetailedErrors on
  IsDevelopment so production circuits surface a generic error and the detail
  is logged server-side only.
- Map tile proxy (the hottest path): stop buffering each tile into a byte[]
  and dropping upstream caching headers. Read response headers only, stream
  the body straight to the browser, forward the upstream caching/validator
  headers (Cache-Control/ETag/Expires/Last-Modified/Vary/Age) with an
  immutable long max-age fallback, forward the browser's conditional headers
  so the upstream can answer 304, and pass 304 through. Browsers can now
  cache tiles instead of re-fetching every tile through the admin-keyed proxy
  on every view.

Adds Docker-free tests for the new cache-header forwarding helpers.
